{"title":"1977 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8556c77243012e5fadde8018ac9a69c925b76c06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{[}x\\textbf{]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> be the largest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> \n(i.e., the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/0/c5034eff1e9eda1278f19c4be405d645e65fdee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le x&lt;n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />). Which of the following statements is (are) true?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7d69015090800f2c205fd8b32ad2666741fed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{I. [}x+1\\textbf{]}=\\textbf{[}x\\textbf{]}+1\\text{ for all }x \\\\ \\textbf{II. [}x+y\\textbf{]}=\\textbf{[}x\\textbf{]}+\\textbf{[}y\\textbf{]}\\text{ for all }x\\text{ and }y \\\\ \\textbf{III. [}xy\\textbf{]}=\\textbf{[}x\\textbf{]}\\textbf{[}y\\textbf{]}\\text{ for all }x\\text{ and }y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"278\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c1201aa46be6e0b8714e3415bdacc7b5d885e8ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\text{none}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\textbf{I }\\text{only}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\textbf{I}\\text{ and }\\textbf{II}\\text{ only}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\textbf{III }\\text{only}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{all}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"560\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8556c77243012e5fadde8018ac9a69c925b76c06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{[}x\\textbf{]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d65a668bf39f54ca65c6875228e22fa102c296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor x \\right \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9c009d622ad76a8f8dd51d14efb342bdf00c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{I}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\" /> is true, as adding by one does not change the fraction part of the number. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b7d9ea23c927b5f89556a78ccb5b2dc0c1e0a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{II}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is false, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c64c0c278df1a4308cf971b74c76904bd4117db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{[}x+y\\textbf{]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> does not always equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f1e7eed3e8356ca6a0243256930742f7a069a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{[}x\\textbf{]}+\\textbf{[}y\\textbf{]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> (If both numbers were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/15001fcbdd6572dd941238f10ff8bfb1037fd6bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{[}1.5+1.5\\textbf{]} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/74960ba99426f4c565aeb339733fd3331e1e61c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{[}1.5\\textbf{]}+\\textbf{[}1.5\\textbf{]} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" />). Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9c009d622ad76a8f8dd51d14efb342bdf00c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{I}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"7\" height=\"12\" /> is true and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b7d9ea23c927b5f89556a78ccb5b2dc0c1e0a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{II}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is false, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2de6291a7e9fa328da202a34bb60bdcf7d1d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\textbf{I }\\text{only}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172330\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 76/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4037/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15177:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172330 and revision id 81211. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}